---
import DesignLayout from '../../layouts/DesignLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/v2/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/v2/SiteFooter.astro';
import { notebookPages, pad2 } from '../../data/notebook-pages';

const page = notebookPages.find((p) => p.number === 10)!;
const next = notebookPages.filter((p) => [12, 13, 8].includes(p.number));
---
<DesignLayout title="Imposter Syndrome ≡ Self-Awareness · Design direction 01 · AWJ">
  <SiteHeader />

  <main>
    <article class="entry">
      <header class="entry__head nb-shell">
        <p class="entry__meta nb-meta">
          <span>AWJ No. {pad2(page.number)}</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span class="nb-pill nb-pill--human">Human</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span>Filed 29 November 2025</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span>3 min read</span>
        </p>
        <figure class="entry__page">
          <div class="nb-page nb-page--lift">
            <img src={page.src} alt={page.alt} width="1600" height="1121" />
          </div>
        </figure>
        <h1 class="entry__title">Imposter Syndrome ≡ Self-Awareness</h1>
        <p class="nb-lede">Only the self-aware suffer from imposter syndrome. Which means the feeling is evidence of something good.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="entry__body nb-shell">
        <div class="nb-prose">
          <p>Only the self-aware suffer from imposter syndrome.</p>
          <p>Everyone I have spoken to about this observation agrees. But it focuses too much on the syndrome and not enough on the imposters that cause it.</p>
          <p>I am not talking about people with imposter syndrome as the imposters. I am talking about the actual imposters, the reason self-aware people get imposter syndrome in the first place.</p>
          <p>Without them, the people overselling themselves, claiming success they did not authentically achieve, bigging themselves up beyond their worth, there would be no imposter syndrome.</p>
          <p>Think about it. When you feel it, you worry that people are judging you. Who does he think he is? He should not be in this room. Clearly he is out of his depth.</p>
          <p>You only think that because you know it is what people think about actual imposters. Not you.</p>
          <blockquote>By virtue of having imposter syndrome, you are not an imposter. It would not be a syndrome if you were.</blockquote>
          <p>As a self-aware person, you only get imposter syndrome when you are growing. It is the uncertainty of growing into the uncharted territory of your potential that brings it on. And that is okay, as long as you are kind to yourself and do not let it hold you back.</p>
          <p>Your imposter syndrome is a skill. A strength. An indicator of your <span class="nb-hl">emotional intelligence</span>.</p>
          <p>In an ever more inauthentic world, where unearned egos go unchecked, your authenticity will become your number one intangible asset.</p>
          <p class="nb-ps">P.S. Does anyone else's spelling go out of the window when they are concentrating on their handwriting?</p>
        </div>

        <aside class="entry__side">
          <div class="side-card">
            <p class="nb-eyebrow">Watch</p>
            <a class="side-video" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N9RxVQCvcpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <img src="https://i.ytimg.com/vi/N9RxVQCvcpg/hqdefault.jpg" alt="Andy Whyte on imposter syndrome, video thumbnail" loading="lazy" />
              <span class="side-video__play" aria-hidden="true">&#9654;</span>
            </a>
            <p class="nb-meta">The 90-second version, filmed over the notebook.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="side-card">
            <p class="nb-eyebrow">Part of</p>
            <a class="side-link" href="#">Imposter syndrome: the hub &rarr;</a>
            <p class="nb-meta">Essays, questions answered and the talk, in one place.</p>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>

      <footer class="entry__foot nb-shell">
        <div class="author">
          <img class="author__photo" src="/media/portrait/andy-portrait.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" />
          <div>
            <p class="author__name">Andy Whyte</p>
            <p class="nb-meta">Founder and CEO of MEDDICC. Author of the best-selling book on sales qualification. Twenty years in sales, one blue notebook.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </article>

    <section class="nb-section nb-section--tint">
      <div class="nb-shell">
        <div class="nb-section-head">
          <p class="nb-eyebrow">Next in the notebook</p>
          <h2>Keep turning.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="nb-grid nb-grid--3">
          {next.map((p) => (
            <a class="next-card" href={p.href}>
              <div class="nb-page"><img src={p.src} alt={p.alt} loading="lazy" /></div>
              <p class="nb-meta">No. {pad2(p.number)}</p>
              <h3>{p.title}</h3>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</DesignLayout>

<style>
  .entry { padding-top: clamp(24px, 4vw, 56px); }
  .entry__head { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; text-align: center; gap: 18px; }
  .entry__meta { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; }
  .entry__page { margin: 8px 0 12px; width: min(760px, 100%); }
  .entry__title { font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 48px); max-width: 20ch; }
  .entry__head .nb-lede { text-align: center; }

  .entry__body { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 66ch) 280px; gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 80px); justify-content: center; margin-top: clamp(32px, 5vw, 64px); }
  .entry__side { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; }
  .side-card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; padding: 18px; border: 1px solid var(--nb-line); border-radius: var(--radius-ui); background: #fff; }
  .side-video { position: relative; display: block; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; background: var(--nb-text); }
  .side-video img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; opacity: .9; }
  .side-video__play { position: absolute; inset: 0; margin: auto; width: 48px; height: 48px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--nb-yellow); color: var(--nb-text); display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: 16px; padding-left: 3px; box-shadow: 0 6px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.25); }
  .side-link { font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .entry__body { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } .entry__side { flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; } .side-card { flex: 1 1 260px; } }

  .entry__foot { margin-top: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px); display: flex; justify-content: center; }
  .author { display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: center; max-width: 66ch; padding-top: 28px; border-top: 1px solid var(--nb-line); width: 100%; }
  .author__photo { width: 64px; height: 64px; border-radius: 999px; object-fit: cover; flex: none; }
  .author__name { font-weight: 600; }

  .next-card { text-decoration: none; color: inherit; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
  .next-card .nb-page { transition: transform .25s var(--ease-out), box-shadow .25s var(--ease-out); }
  .next-card:hover .nb-page { transform: translateY(-4px) rotate(-.4deg); box-shadow: var(--shadow-lift); }
  .next-card h3 { font-size: 18px; }
</style>
